10078	{"artifactId":"LLD-7405471c72bd3e88-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-7405471c72bd3e88-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:23:43.996Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers every part of ISSUE-7405471c's fix intent: port the mocks' stylesheet into BOARD_STYLE with --vscode-* colours, align the webview markup screen by screen, group Issues into the board's collapsible stage sections with the same defaults, keep the live region and density visible but unobtrusive, and compare headless-Chrome screenshots at 1200/600/360 px.","evidence":"ISSUE.md 'Fix intent' lists these four bullets. The LLD covers each one: §2.4 BOARD_STYLE (the mocks' product rules from .appbar to .center, mapped to theme variables); §2.5 BOARD_WEBVIEW_SCRIPT (mocks' markup per screen); §2.1/§3.1–3.3 IssueSectionView, built by the shared sectionDefaults/foldOf; §2.3 footer.foot holding #announce and a small segmented density control; §5 smoke level and migration step 4 (screenshots at 1200, 600 and 360 px). The 'What stays' list (CSP, textContent, no hiding rules, one live region, both densities, 1 s / 150 ms targets) is restated in §4 invariants c1–c5. [files: docs/standalone/defect-delivery-board-shipped-issue-348d4663-E202610107405471c/ISSUE.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the section defaults (open, emptyText, hint) and the fold text are computed inline in buildBoardViewModel, and IssuesBody carries one flat, stage-sorted issues array.","evidence":"board-model.ts:307-324 computes `defaultOpen = all.length > 0 && (stage !== 'complete' || attentionOnly)`, `emptyText`, `hint: !defaultOpen && all.length>0 && needing>0 ? attentionLabel(needing) : null` and foldText inline. Line 333 has `fold: { always: attentionOnly, text: foldText }`. board-protocol.ts:243-248 has `IssuesBody { kind:'issues'; totalsLabel; issues: readonly IssueEntryView[]; emptyPanel }`. board-views.ts:107-110 stable-sorts the issue matches by STAGE_ORDER rank. board-host.ts:427 places `<p id=\"announce\" ... aria-live=\"polite\">` after the app bar, and lines 423-425 render two full density buttons. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-model.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The mocks' product rules contain exactly three content-hiding rules (the details marker, the segmented group's overflow:hidden, and the narrow wordmark). Every other hiding rule belongs to the gallery chrome (.screen, .tab).","evidence":"A search of delivery-board-screen-mocks.html for hiding rules finds: line 35 `.screen{display:none}` (gallery), line 53 `.tab{...overflow:hidden...box-shadow:rgba(...)}` (gallery), line 72 `.seg{...overflow:hidden}`, line 97 `.acc>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}`, line 157 `.crumbs .wordmark{display:none}`. The last three are exactly the design's three replacements. The only non-var colour in the product range is absent: the rgba is on .tab, which is excluded. [files: docs/plans/delivery-board-screen-mocks.html]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The readers of IssuesBody.issues that must change are board-views.ts (builder), board-state.ts (the issue screen's entry lookup) and board-host.ts (the webview's renderIssues). The list is complete.","evidence":"A search for `.issues` and IssuesBody in vscode-plugin/src finds: board-views.ts:104-139 (builder), board-state.ts:399 `buildIssueView(...).issues.find(e => e.card.itemId === item.id)` (covered by 'look the issue screen's entry up across the sections'), board-host.ts:185 `for(const e of b.issues)` (renderIssues, rewritten in §2.5), and board-views.test.ts:78,165-198 (covered by migration step 4's test rewrite). There are no other production readers. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-views.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Removing the h1 from list screens keeps the restore-focus behaviour 'as today' ('a restored screen restores scroll and focuses its opener').","evidence":"board-host.ts:260-262: `const h=head.querySelectorAll('h1.screen-title')[0]; if(m.restored){...const o=...findKey(bodyEl,'item-'+m.focusItemId)||findKey(bodyEl,'epic-'+m.focusItemId);(o||h).focus();} else{...h.focus();}`. Today a restored screen whose opener is no longer shown (for example, after a refresh the opened item no longer matches the filter) falls back to the h1. The design removes the h1 from the four list screens and only names a new focus target for fresh screens (the chosen view button). It does not name the fallback for a restored list screen with no opener. Built as written, `h` is undefined there, and `(o||h).focus()` throws a TypeError, so the rest of render is skipped. The title-update branch at line 254 also keys on h1.screen-title. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"State the restore fallback for list screens (the chosen view button, as for a fresh list screen) in §2.5's postconditions, and add a test: Back to a list screen whose opener no longer matches.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Porting the mocks' rules 'with the same selectors and values', with #main as the inline-size container, reproduces the mocks' narrow layouts.","evidence":"In the mocks the container is the gallery's .tab (line 53 `container-type:inline-size`), and .body is a descendant of it. The design makes #main (which is also `main#main.body`) the container. A container query cannot style the container element itself, so `@container (max-width:480px){ .body{padding:12px} }` (mocks line 160) would never apply. Also, `.seg a{padding:4px 9px}` (line 159) targets anchors, while the design's nav.seg holds four buttons, so a verbatim copy of that rule matches nothing. The narrow layout would then differ from mock 11/360 px. [files: docs/plans/delivery-board-screen-mocks.html]","action":"Make the container a wrapper around main.body (or the body element), or restate the .body padding rule outside the container query. Retarget `.seg a` to `.seg button` in the port.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac4 (Issues grouped by stage) is proved by tests that fail without the fix, and the no-hiding style check that ac1 relies on already exists to be extended.","evidence":"IssuesBody has no `sections` field today (board-protocol.ts:243-248), so the named board-views.test.ts test ('groups issues into stage sections…') and the board-host 'collapsible stage boxes' test cannot pass without the change. board-host.test.ts:1346 already scans BOARD_STYLE for `/display:\\s*none/, /visibility:\\s*hidden/, /clip/, /text-overflow/, /overflow:\\s*hidden/, /height:\\s*0[;}]/`, matching invariant c4. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-views.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac6's proving test, the existing perf test, covers the Issues screen, as §5 states ('including the Issues screen').","evidence":"board-perf.test.ts:56 is the test the design maps to ac6 ('a 500-item, 1,000-record board renders within one second…'). A search of board-perf.test.ts for 'issues' finds no match, so the test never opens the Issues screen today. The acceptance mapping cites this existing title unchanged, so the new sectioned Issues render would not be timed unless the test is extended. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-perf.test.ts]","action":"In §5, name the extension explicitly: board-perf.test.ts switches to the Issues view and asserts the 150 ms target.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-10T07:23:43.996Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"preserved-behaviour.1":{"findingId":"preserved-behaviour.1","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §2.5 postconditions now name the restore fallback (chosen view button on list screens, h1 elsewhere) and title updates no longer key on h1.screen-title; a Back-with-gone-opener test is added.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T07:25:33.772Z"},"preserved-behaviour.2":{"findingId":"preserved-behaviour.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §2.4 makes a div.page wrapper the inline-size container so the .body padding rule applies, and retargets .seg a to .seg button; a test pins both.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T07:25:33.773Z"},"tests.2":{"findingId":"tests.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §5 extends board-perf.test.ts to switch to the Issues view and assert 150 ms; added to ac6.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T07:25:33.773Z"}}}}}}
